"text": "Test Commands, and what is absent: - **Live smoke:** the harness lifecycle, unchanged in shape; `run --perf` also boots and cleans a real session of   its own. - **Headful self-verify:** none exists (no UI surface until Epoch 8). - **Mutation:** scoped inner loops over the four Rust files, then the pre-push's two legs and union. The seam's line   compiles only under `fake-agent`, which every mutation build carries (`run/mutants.rs:152`, :164–165). - **One-shot controls:** the G2 script's `--probe` is its own known-positive, a listed gate. The seam's remove-the-guard   run (neutralise the panic statement, show the forced-panic case red, restore) runs once at implement, with both   readings in `evidence/seam-guard.md` (testing.md 2026-09-25). - **The perf verdict on three OSes** is read through the operator's CI entry; locally it runs on this host only."
}
